 Time-Based Assessment Validation Flaw
 Domain:"confedential".etutor.co

> Security research conducted during an authorized assessment of a web-based examination platform.

 Overview

During an authorized security assessment of a web-based examination platform, I identified an inconsistency in the server-side validation of assessment timing.

The application initially identified an assessment as expired and displayed a remaining duration of `0 Minutes`. The server also returned a negative remaining-time value and triggered an expiration warning.

During further analysis of the application's time-validation requests and responses, I observed that the same assessment could subsequently return a positive remaining-time value. The application then allowed the assessment interface to become accessible again.

This indicates a potential weakness in the enforcement of time-based access controls.

