14. Security Principles Demonstrated

This research demonstrates several important web application security principles.

Server-side enforcement

Security decisions must be enforced by the backend.

Client-side controls are not security boundaries

A browser timer or JavaScript variable should never be considered sufficient protection for a security-sensitive time restriction.

Authoritative time

Time-based authorization should use a trusted server-side clock.

Consistent state management

Security-sensitive state transitions must be validated by the backend.

HTTP request analysis

Inspecting application requests and responses can reveal security-relevant behaviour that may not be visible through the normal user interface.

Secure evidence handling

Security research should be documented without exposing authentication credentials, session tokens, or unnecessary personal information.

